# Ordinary Go ignores.
#
# This replaced a root allowlist that existed only for the design effort, which
# ended when ADR-0001 through ADR-0014 were all Accepted. That file denied the
# repository root by default, so it would have rejected a go.mod (#64).

# Build and test output.
*.test
*.out
*.prof
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
coverage.html

# A binary named after its own directory carries no extension, so no pattern
# anyone would think to write catches it: a 4.3 MB one reached main in PR #24
# and had to be purged by a history rewrite. That is what the allowlist existed
# for, and the replacement is to name the ones this repository can produce.
# Adding a module means adding a line here.
/ferry
/driver/env/env
/driver/kv/kv
/driver/yaml/yaml

# The workspace is checked in and no `replace` directive ever is (ADR-0002).
# Its sum file is generated.
go.work.sum

# Prototypes are scratch and never merge (AGENTS.md, issue #1).
/proto/
